===Climate===
[[File:Ogasawara Tropical Beach.jpg|thumb|left|250px|A tropical beach on Hahajima, with the coral reef visible beneath the crystal-clear waters.]]

Ogasawara Prefecture has a tropical rainforest climate (Köppen climate classification ''Af''), the only prefecture in Okaiken with a truly tropical climate. The islands experience warm to hot temperatures year-round, with no true winter. The average annual temperature is approximately 23 °C (73 °F), and the temperature rarely falls below 15 °C (59 °F) even in the coolest months. The northernmost point of the prefecture, [[Touga]], sits at approximately 11.66°S latitude — the northernmost tropical territory in Okaiken.

The climate is shaped by the warm [[Aishio Current]] that flows past the islands, maintaining sea surface temperatures above 25 °C year-round and supporting the coral reef ecosystems. The prefecture lies within the typhoon belt, and severe tropical storms strike between November and April, with the peak season in January and February.

